ays  been clear your thoughts  the president doesn't have the mandate  to do this  because during the campaign what he was  telling voters was  the opposite position he can't claim  that the voters elected him to pack the  courts  president biden as a candidate was  essentially promising not to do this  and what what did president trump do by  appointing the supreme court justices  it was his job there were vacancies  and he put forward nominees who got  confirmed  and furthermore president biden in what  they want is  what he wants as far as a vision for the  court is now talking about our  rights not being absolute in the  constitution even though of course  constitution uses words like  shall not be infringed and president  biden's indicating that  that shall be infringed yes he's open  only some are absolute but not the ones  he likes  uh greg you know justice stephen breyer  uh this week  issued this stark warning to democrats  on court packing listen to this  what i'm trying to do is to make those  whose initial instincts may favor  important structural change or other  similar institutional changes  such as forms of court packing think  long and hard  before they embody those changes in law  structural  alteration motivated by the perception  of political influence can only feed  that latter perception i'm either  eroding that trust  i mean greg he knew exactly what he was  saying ruth bader ginsburg said the same  thing  folks on the left are calling for him to  step down because they want a  replacement now  what's going to happen here well it's a  tortured fantasy  packing the supreme court and it won't  happen and the reason is pretty simple  to accomplish it democrats would have to  kill the filibuster and they don't have  the votes to do that  look joe biden is now officially and  clearly  surrendered to the progressive woke  crowd  led by his vice president the locust of  the woke  there's a reason why breyer and ginsburg  were against this and that's 